 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Use Graphs <i>I</i> and <i>J</i> in Figure 12.212 to answer each question.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 543313,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which vertices are in each of the components that remain when edge <i>jl</i> is removed from Graph <i>J</i>?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Removing <i>ji</i> breaks the tree into two separate components so that it is no longer a tree.</p>\n<p>One component: <i>g, h, i, j</i></p>\n<p>The other component: <i>k, l, m</i></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Vertices <i>k, l</i>, and <i>m</i> are in one component, and vertices <i>g, h, i</i>, and <i>j</i> are in the other."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 543314,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Determine the number of edges and the number of vertices in Graph <i>I</i>. Explain how this confirms that Graph <i>I</i> is a tree.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The number of edges in a tree graph with <i>n</i> vertices is <i>n</i> – 1.</p>\n<p>This graph has 6 vertices and 5 edges. This is what the formula predicts for a tree graph with 6 vertices. If <i>n</i> is 6, then <i>n</i> – 1 is 5.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "There are 6 vertices and 5 edges, which confirms Graph <i>I</i> is a tree, because the number of edges is one less than the number of vertices."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 543315,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What kind of cycle is created if edge <i>cf</i> is added to Graph <i>I</i>?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "If you add edge <i>cf,</i> then you will have a quadrilateral (<i>b, c, f, e</i>)."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "a quadrilateral"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
